    dispersion (5); plus the dots (1). Review candidates, to evaluate not
    decide: (1) control-object grouping - bart2 does NOT take a control =
    formal today (unlike xbart's control = dbarts::dbartsControl(),
    R/xbart.R:23); it instead reconstructs one internally via
    redirectCall(matchedCall, dbarts::dbartsControl) (R/bart.R:637),
    backfilling any bart2 formal that shares a dbartsControl slot name from
    bart2's own default (R/bart.R:638-650), and validates unknown
    top-level args against the union of bart2's and dbartsControl's formals
    (R/bart.R:626-628); 13 of the 52 (verbose, keepTrainingFits,
    useQuantiles, keepTrees, n.samples, n.cuts, n.burn, n.trees, n.chains,
    n.threads, n.thin, printEvery, printCutoffs) are already 1:1
    dbartsControl slots by name, so a control = formal (xbart's shape) is
    the most direct candidate. (2) prior/spec-object grouping - forest()'s
    declaration vocabulary (R/model.R:1545-1572: basis, vars, n.trees,
    base, power, sd, interactions, blocks, amplitude.prior.variance,
    update.amplitude) already covers per-forest n.trees/base/power/
    interactions/blocks generically; the variance forest's four flat args
    (variance, n.trees.variance, power.variance, base.variance,
    R/bart.R:549-552) are the in-package precedent for a flat quartet that
    could become one object. (3) formula-carried structure - representing
    constraints/priors as formula terms rather than flat arguments.
    Interacts with the K-forest front-door DOOR: whether bart2 gains
    multi-forest reach via a forests = flat formal (drafted as
    bcf-s5-relocation's D1, "forests = NULL as a bart2 formal",
    design-draft.md:848,853-856) or via formula-level term syntax is
    undecided per VD's 2026-08-15 bcf-s5-relocation walkthrough (Fork A
    CONCURs D1 schedules independently on dbarts' own merits,
    critique-round1.md:622,629-631); arc records in
    .claude/bcf-s5-relocation/, spec commit into docs/plans pending.
