  bcf-sigma-tail-mixing: OPTIONAL research door (docs/plans/bcf-sigma-
    residual.md sec 4 item 2; no separate plan doc). Open: the EXTREME
    tail (|a0| >= ~40, ~3% of the prior) is frozen-structure mixing
    that no amount of burn fixes; a principled remedy would target
    tree-structure mixing at high SNR (tempered early sweeps,
    restart-style grow proposals). Low priority - the regime only
    arises with a stale build scale swapped against a new response
    inside a larger Gibbs loop (setResponse updateScale=FALSE).
    research-open, decision-gated.
  binary-kforest-k1-reachability: K = 1 as a SHIPPED multi-forest
    configuration - one varying-coefficient forest with no prognostic
    partner, which is VCBART's shape (D4 of docs/design/model-space-
    survey.md). Today it is a designed refusal (spec.R, added by
    binary-kforest-prior-default S2). Priced live rather than
    inherited: the engine already takes it - drawGlue dispatches
    K != 2 to the general drawAmplitudes, synthesizeIndicatorBasis is
    gated on numForests_ > 1, shippedShape() is simply false at K = 1,
    and createBCFSampler imposes no count floor - so this is a bridge
    (applyBCFSpec's Rf_xlength < 2) plus R change with tests, NOT
    engine work. Gated on ACCEPTANCE EVIDENCE: a new shipped
    configuration owes its own, which is why S2 refused rather than
    opened it.
