  host-shell-read-guards: bart2's multinomial (and, once
    adoption-slate S7 lands, its ordinal and nbinom) fits carry a
    placeholder $fit host sampler whose hostFor field makes MUTATION
    refuse (refuseHostMutation, R/dbarts.R). READS do not:
    $getLatents, $getForestFits, $getSigmas and $getCalibration all
    answer from the shell, which carries the design and priors the fit
    was built from but not its model. adoption-slate S1 adds a
    read-side sibling for the ONE new accessor it introduces
    ($getFitsWithoutOffset) and deliberately leaves the four shipped
    readers alone, since changing a shipped reader is outside that
    slice. The open question, carried to VD 2026-08-15 and TICKETED
    rather than built: should every read on a host shell refuse, or
    only those whose value is structurally wrong there? They are not
    equal - $getSigmas returns a real sigma of a real sampler, just
    not the one the user fit, while $getForestFits returns fits of a
    forest that never participated. If "all": rename or generalize
    refuseHostMutation, four call sites, four Rd sentences, four
    cells, ~20 non-test / ~35 test raw additions. Pre-release at
    discretion.
