  setpredictor-dimnames: a whole-matrix transactional (or forced)
    setPredictor(x, ...) installs x into sampler$data@x as a plain
    matrix, dropping x's column names even when the sampler was built
    with named columns (pre-existing since
    docs/plans/multiforest-predictor-mutation.md S1). Breaks by-name
    column resolution on every later call that resolves a column by
    name against that sampler - most visibly
    updatePredictorPerObservationJointly's shared-column match.
    Workaround documented (man/dbartsSampler-class.Rd,
    man/updatePredictorPerObservationJointly.Rd): mutate a column at a
    time (setPredictor(x, column = ...)), which preserves dimnames via
    installPredictorColumns' in-place assignment, or order any joint
    call before the whole-matrix replacement. Small R-layer fix:
    carry the incoming x's dimnames (or fall back to the existing
    matrix's) when building the replacement. Not scheduled; small
    slice, no plan doc yet.
